MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_001: Hmm, yes... It seems the wild wind has a want to\nguide me.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_002: Mmm. Your words are untrue, Syracusio.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_003: I once told you—don't speak of the spirits in your\nnonsensical way. They find it confusing.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_004: Now, now. Nothing I said about the wind was meant\nas an offense to your otherworldly friends.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_005: When I speak, I allow my poetic instincts to take\nmy words where they want to go. That is all.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_006: But please, could you refrain from speaking my\nname in public? I go by Sirocco these days.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_007: Yes, I will refrain. I ask that you also refrain...from\nwords that roil the spirits.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_008: I fail to see how my mention of the wind would\ntrouble the spirits. But it doesn't matter.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_009: I must tell you, you have not changed. You are just as\nbeautiful and mysterious as the first day I met you.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_010: You have also not changed.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_011: I suspect you mean that quite differently than I do.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_012: You know, I was only 15 that day I met you on\nthe battlefield.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_013: I'd been made a vulkan barely more than a year\nbefore. I was just a minor celestial general then.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_014: I'd like to think I'm a fair sight more refined now.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_015: Is that...true? You seem exactly the same to me.\nI remember what you said on that day.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_016: No, please don't. I'd prefer not to hear you repeat\nthe words I said to you.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_017: Hm? But...why not?
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_018: I was young and immature when I tried to speak\nto you about my love.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_019: I didn't know you were Black-Lace Ninae, a\nchief celestial general—feared even among vulkans.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_020: After you dismissed me so coldly, I became the\nlaughingstock of the camp.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_021: So, I'd rather not be reminded of that time. Now,\nI think I'll excuse myself.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_C_022: Coldly... How strange Syracusio is.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_001: Yes...perhaps it's time to move on.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_002: For a new breeze to blow...an old love must go.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_003: Wait, Syracusio.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_004: I am drawn on that paper. Why are you trying to\ntear it up?
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_005: You must have quite an eye for art if you could tell\nwhat was drawn on the page after only a glance.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_006: Most people don't seem to understand my sketches...\nBut perhaps you like this one?
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_007: I myself have difficulty understanding the appeal.\nBut the spirits—they like that drawing.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_008: Ah, I see. The spirits like it. Of course.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_009: All these years later, you still dislike the Fiery Wind.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_010: Dislike... I have never felt that way about you.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_011: What do you mean? You were so very cold to me\nwhen I was 15.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_012: I was a different Ninae then, one who had an\nunsure grasp of her expressions.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_013: I spoke only to my father and the spirits. In battles, I\nsaid nothing—and was called the Angel of Death.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_014: That was my life—put on a pedestal or seen as\na terror. And nothing in between.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_015: That's why I said so little when you spoke to me\nback then. I was unprepared.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_016: Is that so? Haha. I really did lack experience in\nthose days.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_017: I was too captivated by your beauty to see\nyour confusion.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_018: I think I'll let this drawing remain intact. It seems\nto me now...this night is ours.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_019: Ours? But the night belongs to no one.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_020: Not to worry. This searing wind will take possession\nof it and make it yours and mine alone.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_021: And I'm not talking about your spirit companions.\nI mean the breeze that goes by the name Sirocco.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_022: Your meaning eludes me. But I know this. I sense\nwarmth under your words, as I did years ago.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_023: Hmm, this wind...might it truly be these spirits\nof yours?
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_024: Yes, Syracusio. And they want a closer look at\nyour drawing.
MID_SE_Nin_Sci_B_025: Of course. As they wish.